    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0805" n="711" xml:id="pg711"/>

                <head>No. 451.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 12, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 114.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your No. 70, of date March 30, relative to the alleged discrimination against
                    the United States carrying trade, and have to say in reply that no
                    correspondence has taken place between the Mexican Government and this legation
                    since Mr. Mariscal’s note to me of February 21 until to-day, when I addressed
                    him a note, copy of which I herewith inclose.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Manning</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d451-a1.xml" xpointer="d451-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
